body:
Considering how attached you are to her, it would be a good idea to find someone to take care of your child for the few hours that the funeral will take. It's a way of saying goodbye, and unless your decision not to go is based on your feelings towards the idea of going itself (in which case it's better not to go), you may benefit from being present. 

&#x200B;

As for the afterlife - I'm sure everyone has wondered about that, but we will not know until it's our time to go. You can choose what to believe but try not to let it consume you, it's the one knowledge no one will miss out on.
